s.\n`WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, up to 3 attempts in total. I tested it against a real local HTTP server and it behaved as intended.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `urlopen` raises `HTTPError` on a 503. The client catches it, closes the error response and waits before trying again. The wait doubles each time: `backoff * 2**attempt`, so 0.5s and then 1s with the default setting.\n- If the 3rd attempt also gets a 503, that `HTTPError` is raised to the caller.\n- Other HTTP errors are raised straight away with no retry. Network failures and timeouts (`URLError`) are not retried either, since you only asked for 503.\n- Two new optional constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`, set the attempt count and wait time. Existing calls don't need to change.\n\n**Test results** (test server with backoff set to 0.01s):\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| Succeeds first time | `{'temp': 20}` | 1 |\n| 503 twice, then 200 | `{'temp': 20}` | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I haven't added a test file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35283, "requests_cache_write": 142515, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7520196, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1617, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial7", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 72, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:47:43.758862+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.629, "t_checker_s": 1.92, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "n